ower Plant in Khuzestan. The program’s research capabilities are anchored by several facilities, most notably the Tehran Research Reactor and the heavy water reactor at Khondab. Iran's uranium processing infrastructure is centered in Isfahan, which serves as a hub for conversion and fuel fabrication, while primary enrichment activities are conducted at Natanz, Fordow, and within the Isfahan complex.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_program_of_Iran","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"places":[{"title":"United States","extract":"The United States of America (USA), also known as the United States (U.S.) or America, is a country primarily located in North America. It is a federal republic consisting of 50 states and a federal capital district, Washington, D.C. The 48 contiguous states border Canada to the north and Mexico to the south, with the semi-exclave of Alaska in the northwest and the archipelago of Hawaii in the Pacific Ocean. The United States also asserts sovereignty over five major island territories and various uninhabited islands in Oceania and the Caribbean. It is a megadiverse country, with the world's fourth-largest total area and third-largest population, exceeding 341 million.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"US"},{"title":"Iran","extract":"Iran, officially the Islamic Republic of Iran, and historically known as Persia, is a country in West Asia. It borders Iraq to the west; Turkey, Azerbaijan, and Armenia to the northwest; the Caspian Sea to the north, Turkmenistan to the northeast; Afghanistan to the east; Pakistan to the southeast; and the Gulf of Oman and the Persian Gulf to the south. With a population of over 92 million, Iran ranks 17th globally in both geographic size and population. It is divided into five regions with 31 provinces. Tehran is the nation's capital and largest city and serves as its primary economic center.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"IR"}],"arc":{"reports":32,"first_seen":"2026-10-10T11:07:00Z","first_title":"The Iran war is exposing dangerous gaps in the US military system built to save wounded troops","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimwFBVV95cUxNVDFPM0UtMHhyMTBwQmdxZkdFa2QzU0JabHljN256bnBBWjhBVFh6UDlEb1ZNTkJ5cy14bHJXdnQ0VEVrTm1zMmtQM0J0M2ZQWElBbXcwWmlOM3lPOVpERFZzTzMxYjE0RVNidzZJRV9aM2I2YWxRTVlwSEdSTDJ0R0FCS2x1Tk1MZ0dFYkc2U0hzbVZlS0FCOF9sbw?oc=5","first_publisher":"Business Insider","earlier":[{"id":"e_233c8865ec1c","title":"Trump rules out using a nuclear bomb on Iran: Why that matters","date":"2026-10-16T10:21:12Z","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/16/trump-rules-out-using-a-nuclear-bomb-on-iran-why-that-matters?traffic_source=rss","publisher":"Al Jazeera English","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_9c75e6346184","title":"Stocks Tick Up As Trump Downplays Ground Troops In Iran","date":"2026-10-16T12:00:25Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijAFBVV95cUxObWVhZ0FOdzAzU1JSSDM4NVRjbVpxaVJFMW9jd3RxUHVTRUVQQ3NrbTR6dzVtYkNaSXNEQzZQamk4aXJTdTZ3NG5vZi1rVGFMamp6cTIybXNfTm1NYllCdm42M21xdXRNTWRwOGtsWm5ON29aSUNieWNGSnk3Szk4Z0ZRcllhZnNzWHF0Vg?oc=5","publisher":"Finimize","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_cf3beb6b908f","title":"Trump rules out US troops in Iran, leaves Pickaxe Mountain strike on the table","date":"2026-10-16T14:24:45Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPcjh3R0FKTGk2S1V0SUw3LUphVGhnazVNTTNlNzNLMGJsclJvZXRJZmFvZEdWbUNfal9UZ1lucW55Xy1WVDVoM2xoajEzRWRzVW1mck5NbE1VaFR6b3FDRURpaXZlR1NqOVNkVkZmZk93ekUyOVUzTjJ1b2tJRUhCNnNBWG1OczY5R3kwb0Z2SXM5ZnV1MUJjS0t2ZFhUN1cyc1lXbmNNVURQTU53VF8wREhn?oc=5","publisher":"Al-Monitor","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_608ad74c5ba7","title":"Trump says no nukes or ground troops for Iran, weighs in on MOAB as Hormuz risks rise","date":"2026-10-16T17:28:32Z","url":"https://news.google.c